Class AAMotionAPI.GearMotionConfig (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): One electronic-gearing motion: the axis follows a master parameter multiplied by RatioNumerator / RatioDenominator.
Signature: class AAMotion.AAMotionAPI+GearMotionConfig

Members:
- ctor .ctor()
- property System.Int32 Filter { get; set; }
  Input filter in 64ths (MasterFilt), 1 to 64: 64 passes the geared master unfiltered, a smaller value filters more slowly. Direct gearing only; indirect gearing leaves MasterFilt alone.
- property System.String Master { get; set; }
  The parameter the axis follows, named with its axis prefix: "BPos" (B's encoder), "APosRef" (A's position command), "AAuxPos", "AVel[2]".
- property System.Int32 MasterModRev { get; set; }
  The master's modulus (MasterModRev): the master's own ModRev when it has one, 0 for none.
- property System.Int32 MotionMode { get; set; }
  GearDirect (5) or GearIndirect (6).
- property System.Int32 RatioDenominator { get; set; }
  Ratio denominator (MasterFactDen), 1 to 16777215 on 5.3 firmware. Firmware without MasterFactDen divides by 65536 and takes only 65536 here.
- property System.Int32 RatioNumerator { get; set; }
  Ratio numerator (MasterFact), in the range the controller gives it (-16777215 to 16777215 on 5.3 firmware).

Class AAMotionAPI.SinePtpMotionConfig (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): The complete kinematic parameter set of one AXM Sine PTP motion (MotionMode 20/21).
Signature: class AAMotion.AAMotionAPI+SinePtpMotionConfig

Members:
- ctor .ctor()
- property System.Double AbsTrgt { get; set; }
  Absolute motion target, in position units. Used while RelTrgt is 0.
- property System.Double Accel { get; set; }
  Maximum acceleration, in acceleration units.
- property System.Double Decel { get; set; }
  Maximum deceleration, in acceleration units.
- property System.Double JerkInAcc { get; set; }
  Maximum jerk while accelerating, in jerk units.
- property System.Double JerkInDec { get; set; }
  Maximum jerk while decelerating, in jerk units.
- property System.Int32 MotionMode { get; set; }
  20 for a single motion, 21 for a reciprocating one. Ignored by SinePtpCommit.
- property System.Double PreCruAbsTrgt { get; set; }
  Absolute target at which the cruise phase begins. Used while PreCruRelTrgt is 0.
- property System.Double PreCruRelTrgt { get; set; }
  Relative target at which the cruise phase begins. A non-zero value overrides PreCruAbsTrgt.
- property System.Double PreCruiseSpd { get; set; }
  Maximum speed of the pre-cruise phase. 0 disables the pre-cruise phase and the two targets above.
- property System.Double RelTrgt { get; set; }
  Relative motion target, in position units. A non-zero value overrides AbsTrgt.
- property System.Double Speed { get; set; }
  Maximum speed of the cruise phase, in velocity units. Must be non-zero (error 382).

Class AAMotionConfig (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): Global configuration class to control the behavior of AAMotion
Signature: class AAMotion.AAMotionConfig

Members:
- property static System.Int32 FastReadCacheRefreshIntervalMs { get; set; }
  When FastReadCache is enabled, this interval controls how often data is refreshed from the controller. Default: 1ms
- property static System.Boolean FastReadEnabled { get; set; }
  Turns the fast read cache on: every registered keyword is refreshed with one bulk query every FastReadCacheRefreshIntervalMs, MotionStat and InTargetStat last, and reading a registered keyword answers from the cache instead of the controller. Default: false (disabled for backward compatibility).
- property static System.Boolean HighResolutionTimer { get; set; }
  Holds Windows at a 1 ms timer resolution while any controller is connected. Default: false. Takes effect at once, connected or not; on other operating systems it does nothing.
- property static System.Int32 InTargetStatRefreshIntervalMs { get; set; }
  How often, in milliseconds, the fast read cache reads InTargetStat of an axis that is moving, from Begin until the axis reads 4 (in target). Only the moving axes are read: one axis with <axis>InTargetStat, the reply the controller answers fastest (about 0.4–0.7 ms); several with one bulk. Default: 1.
- property static System.Int32 MoveStartConfirmMs { get; set; }
  The longest time, in milliseconds, after Begin that the fast read cache waits to see a motion start before it answers MotionStat and InTargetStat again. Default: 5.

Class AAValueArray (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): Base array wrapper - provides index validation, event triggering and other basic functionality Used for low-level arrays (event-driven) that communicate with controller. Value (on a single-valued parameter), the indexer and enumeration are controller round trips, so the debug view shows the slot's identity only.
