Class ConnectionProbeResult (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): The outcome of ProbeConnection: whether the controller answered a command, how long the round trip took, and when it did not answer, why.
Signature: class AAMotion.ConnectionProbeResult

Members:
- property System.Boolean ControllerRestarted { get; }
  ControllerTime is lower than the previous successful probe on the same connection read, so the controller restarted in between.
- property System.Nullable<System.Int64> ControllerTime { get; }
  The controller's Time, seconds since power-on, when it answered; null otherwise.
- property AAMotion.ConnectionProbeFailure Failure { get; }
  None when IsAlive, otherwise why not.
- property System.Boolean IsAlive { get; }
  The controller answered with a number.
- property System.String Message { get; }
  The error text when the probe failed; null when it succeeded.
- property System.Double RoundTripMs { get; }
  From the call to its reply or failure, in milliseconds, including any wait behind other commands; 0 when the link was down and nothing was sent.
- property System.DateTime Timestamp { get; }
  When the probe finished (UTC).

Class ControllerErrorEventArgs (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): One error ErrorReported reports: everything ErrorOccurred carries, plus which AAMotion member the application called, the axis and parameter the failed command named, where the error came from, and when and on which thread it was raised.
Signature: class AAMotion.ControllerErrorEventArgs

Members:
- property System.Nullable<AAMotion.AxisRef> Axis { get; }
  The axis the failed command names, or null when it names none or Command is not a single controller command.
- property System.String Command { get; }
  The command exactly as sent to the controller (AAbsTrgt=12.5); for a ClientCheck, the name of the method that refused. The same value ErrorOccurred passes.
- property AAMotion.MotionController Controller { get; }
  The controller the error was raised on, which tells several controllers apart.
- property System.Int32 ErrorCode { get; }
  The controller's error code, or -1 for an error AAMotion detected itself; the same value ErrorOccurred passes.
- property System.Nullable<AAMotion.eKeyword> Keyword { get; }
  The parameter the failed command names, or null when it is not one AAMotion knows or Command is not a single controller command.
- property System.String Message { get; }
  The formatted error text; the same value ErrorOccurred passes.
- property System.String Method { get; }
  The outermost public AAMotion member on the call stack, such as SingleAxis.MoveAbs or SingleAxis.Speed (set) for a property write: the member the application called, unless the JIT compiler inlined that member into the application's code, which a Release build does to thin members. It then names a public member the called one calls (MotionController.SendCommandString for AAMotionAPI.SendCommandString). Null for a background read, and when no public AAMotion member is left on the stack.
- property AAMotion.ControllerErrorSource Source { get; }
  Where the error came from: the application's own call, a check before sending, or one of the fast read cache's background reads.
- property System.Int32 ThreadId { get; }
  The managed thread the error was raised on, which is the thread handlers run on: UI code compares it with its own to tell whether it must marshal (Invoke).
- property System.DateTime Timestamp { get; }
  When the error was raised (UTC).

Class HomingDefStep (AAMotion; AAMotion C#): One step of HomingDef. The array is 20 steps of 10 slots: slot 1 holds the step type and slots 2-10 are that type's nine parameters, whose meaning depends on it — a speed, an acceleration, a position offset or a timeout in current-loop samples. HomingDef remains the escape hatch for a firmware step type this SDK does not name.
Signature: class AAMotion.HomingDefStep

Members:
- property System.Double Item[System.Int32] { get; set; }
  Parameter param of the step, 1 to 9.
- field System.Int32 MaxSteps = 20
  Homing steps the firmware executes, matching HOMING_MAXIMUM_STEPS.
- property System.Double Param1 { get; set; }
  First parameter of the step (slot 2).
- property System.Double Param2 { get; set; }
  Second parameter of the step (slot 3).
- property System.Double Param3 { get; set; }
  Third parameter of the step (slot 4).
- property System.Double Param4 { get; set; }
  Fourth parameter of the step (slot 5).
- property System.Double Param5 { get; set; }
  Fifth parameter of the step (slot 6).
- property System.Double Param6 { get; set; }
  Sixth parameter of the step (slot 7).
- property System.Double Param7 { get; set; }
  Seventh parameter of the step (slot 8).
- property System.Double Param8 { get; set; }
  Eighth parameter of the step (slot 9).
- property System.Double Param9 { get; set; }
  Ninth parameter of the step (slot 10).
- field System.Int32 SlotsPerStep = 10
  Slots per homing step, matching the firmware's HOMING_NUM_OF_PARAMS.
- property System.Int32 Step { get; }
  The 1-based step number this view addresses.
- property System.Int32 Type { get; set; }
  The step type in slot 1 — 0 ends the homing routine.

Interface ICiSlave (AAMotion; AAMotion C#).
Signature: interface AAMotion.ICiSlave

Members:
- method System.Boolean CiConnect()
  Connect Central-I device
