  Motion mode, readable and writable. MotionMode determines the type of motion to be executed after the next Begin command. MotionMode cannot be changed until the current motion is finished. MotionMode values and corresponding motion types: 0 - Jog: The motor moves continuously at the speed set by Speed until a Stop command is received. Acceleration and deceleration are controlled by Accel and Decel, and can be smoothed by Jerk.1 - PTP: Point-to-point motion, moves to the position specified by RelTrgt or AbsTrgt (if RelTrgt=0, then AbsTrgt). Parameters are controlled by Accel, Speed, Decel, and Jerk.2 - PTP Repeat: Reciprocating motion between current and target position, waits RptWait time at each end, use StopRep to stop.3 - Pulse/Direction Direct Mode: Position loop reference is directly from pulse/direction input.4 - Pulse/Direction Indirect Mode: Pulses are accumulated to the target, the analyzer generates a smooth trajectory according to Accel, Decel, Speed, and Jerk.5 - Gear Direct Motion6 - Gear Indirect Motion7 - ECAM Direct Motion8 - ECAM Indirect Motion9 - FIFO Motion10 - Follower Position Reference11 - CNC Group A Motion12 - Joystick Direct Motion (analog signal as position reference)13 - Joystick Indirect Motion (analog signal as position reference, analyzer customizable)14 - Joystick Direct Motion (analog signal as speed reference)15 - Joystick Indirect Motion (analog signal as speed reference, analyzer customizable)16 - Vector Motion17 - CNC Group B Motion18 - Spline Buffer Motion20 - Sine PTP: Point-to-point motion on a sinusoidal acceleration profile, controlled by Speed, Accel, Decel, JerkInAcc, JerkInDec and the optional pre-cruise phase (PreCruAbsTrgt/PreCruRelTrgt/PreCruiseSpd).21 - Sine PTP Repeat: Reciprocating motion on a sinusoidal acceleration profile, use StopRep to stop.22 - PVAJ: the axis follows the points of PVAJList, which must be validated (PVAJValidate) and armed (PVAJArm) before Begin.23 - Multi-axis PVAJ: every axis in this mode starts with one Begin as a group, each on its own PVAJList.
- property AAMotion.MotionMode MotionModeEnum { get; }
- property System.Int32 MotionReason { get; }
  Motion failure reason 0: Normal 1: Stop request 2: Abort request 3: Stop reciprocating request 4: Negative limit switch 5: Positive limit switch 6: Negative position limit 7: Positive position limit 8: Unexpected motor disable (see MotorReason command) 9: User request to stop ECAM 10: User request to stop FIFO 11: Reference zero detection 12: User request to stop CNCA 13: Homing timeout 14: Switch to current mode 15: Homing to mechanical limit 16: Zero switch 17: Switch to force control mode 18: CNC participating axis disabled 19: CNC participating axis stopped 20: CNC participating axis aborted 21: Stopped by digital input 22: Aborted by digital input 23: CNCA participating axis triggered positive/negative limit switch 24: CNCA participating axis reached positive/negative position limit 25: User request to stop CNCB 26: CNCB participating axis event 27: CNCB participating axis triggered positive/negative limit switch 28: Stopped by digital input control 29: User request to stop vector motion 30: Vector participating axis disabled 31: Vector participating axis stopped 32: Vector participating axis aborted 33: Vector participating axis triggered positive/negative limit switch 34: Vector participating axis reached positive/negative position limit 35: User request to stop interpolation motion 36: Interpolation participating axis disabled 37: Interpolation participating axis stopped 38: Interpolation participating axis aborted 39: Interpolation participating axis triggered positive/negative limit switch 40: Interpolation participating axis reached positive/negative position limit 41: Jog motion stopped due to exceeding negative or positive position limit
- property AAMotion.MotionReason MotionReasonEnum { get; }
- property AAMotion.AAValueArray<System.Double> MotionSamples { get; }
  Motion time sampling array MotionSamples[1]: Motion profile time; MotionSamples[2]: Profile time + time before reaching target point stability (excluding InTargetTime); MotionSamples[3]: Profile time + time to reach target point stability including InTargetTime; The time is reported in number of controller samples (typically for Agito's controllers: 1/16384=61(s per sample).
- property System.Int32 MotionStat { get; }
  MotionStat reports the status of the current motion. Each bit in MotionStat represents a motion state: Bit 0: In motion Bit 1: Waiting (during repetitive motion) Bit 2: In repetitive stop (following StopRep command) Bit 3: Stop requested Bit 4: In acceleration Bit 5: In deceleration Bit 6: Waiting for smoothing to end Bit 7: In ECAM stop (following StopECAM command) Bit 8: In FIFO stop (following StopFIFO command) Bit 9: In wait for Input (motion is suspended till rising edge at the user defined input) Multiple bits may be set simultaneously. When the motor is not in motion, MotionStat = 0.
- property AAMotion.MotionStat MotionStatEnum { get; }
  The MotionStat register as a bit set: every set bit is the flags member that names it, an unmapped bit is carried as is, and MotionStat.None is no motion. Test a bit with a mask, not with equality.
