Members:
- property System.Int32 PVAJValidate { get; set; }
  PVAJValidate checks the PVAJ list and, when it passes, marks it valid so the axis can be armed. 1 runs the full check: positions inside [RevPLim, FwdPLim], velocities inside MaxVel, accelerations inside MaxAcc, and the continuity of consecutive points against PVAJPosTol and PVAJVelTol. 2 forces the list through unchecked; 3 runs the range checks only. A failure is reported as a controller error naming what failed, for example 393 (position out of range).
- property System.Double PVAJVelTol { get; set; }
  PVAJVelTol is the velocity tolerance of the PVAJ continuity check, in counts/sec. Validation fails with error 397 when a point differs by more than this from the velocity the previous point predicts.
- property System.Double PeakCL { get; set; }
  Peak current limit, readable and writable, in mA. Used to limit the maximum allowable current of the motor/driver (±PeakCL). PeakCL, ContCL and PeakTime are jointly used for I²t power limitation: After the peak current persists for PeakTime, if the square of the integrated current exceeds ContCL², the current limitation is ±ContCL to prevent overload. PeakCL represents the peak value of sinusoidal current and can be dynamically adjusted. The specific status can be queried through bits 24 and 25 of the StatReg register. The value is a double and carries any User-Units scaling AAComm applied to the reply.
- property System.Int32 PeakTime { get; set; }
  Peak current duration, readable and writable. Used together with PeakCL and ContCL for I2t power limiting, unit: ms.
- property System.Int32 PolePrs { get; set; }
  Pole number, readable and writable. represents the number of magnetic pole pairs per mechanical turn of the motor.
